<title>CANADA: Canada to auction C$3.5 bln bonds due 1999.</title>
<headline>Canada to auction C$3.5 bln bonds due 1999.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Government of Canada said it plans to auction on June 11 C$3.5 billion of bonds with an unspecified coupon and maturing on September 15, 1999.</p>
<p>The Bank of Canada will buy a minimum of C$350 million of the new bonds.</p>
<p>The bonds, which will be dated and delivered on June 16, pay interest on September 15 and March 15.  </p>
<p>Proceeds of the issue will used for general purposes.</p>
<p>The government said there were no marketable bonds maturing on June 16.</p>
